[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-378e6e4c-2f4b-42f2-bf5a-8710d3bb34a1\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Papers</p><strong>Mon 17 Nov 2025 14:00 - 14:10 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/ase-2025/ase-2025-venue-grand-hall-3\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Grand Hall 3</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/ase-2025/ase-2025-papers#program\" class=\"navigate\">Formal Method &amp; Verification 1</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/nazarenoaguirre\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Nazareno Aguirre</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"378e6e4c-2f4b-42f2-bf5a-8710d3bb34a1\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>ScaleCirc: Scaling the Analysis over Circom Circuits</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>Zero-knowledge proof (ZKP) circuits implemented in programming languages like Circom are fundamental to blockchain and privacy-preserving applications. These codes often suffer from constraint-related issues where constraints fail to accurately specify intended computations. While existing analysis tools have been proposed, they struggle with large-scale circuits containing complex template embeddings. We present ScaleCirc, a novel framework that addresses such limitations through: 1) systematic management of analysis redundancy via circuit deduplication strategies; 2) constrainedness propagation methods leveraging source code semantic information; and 3) a generalizable framework for different circuit analysis tasks. Evaluation on 691 real-world circuits shows ScaleCirc demonstrates higher efficiency, and successfully analyzes many Circom programs that existing works failed on. We also identified 3 previously unreported under-constrained bugs in the Circomlib library.</p>\n<p></p><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/jinanjiang1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Jinan Jiang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">The Hong Kong Polytechnic University</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/haoranqin\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Haoran Qin<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">The Hong Kong Polytechnic University</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/xiapuluo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Xiapu Luo\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/xiapuluo/5c127a24-da71-4a65-926c-ce8ef3475534/micro-avatar?1783975591000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Xiapu Luo<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Hong Kong Polytechnic University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2025/ase-2025-papers/173/ScaleCirc-Scaling-the-Analysis-over-Circom-Circuits\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-378e6e4c-2f4b-42f2-bf5a-8710d3bb34a1').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
